            <ArticleTitle>Acute bilateral optic disk edema with a macular star figure in a 12-year-old girl.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 12-year-old girl developed headaches and bilateral optic disk edema due to malignant hypertension. Optic disk edema in most of these cases is probably on the spectrum of ischemic optic neuropathy rather than increased intracranial pressure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
